{"id": "EUVD-2026-103309", "enisaUuid": "b566d5b9-c228-38c1-81b1-945de085452a", "description": "phpMyFAQ 4.0.0 before 4.1.9 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability where WebAuthn registration endpoints attach credentials to any account without authentication or challenge validation. Attackers can stage a victim username, submit a forged fmt=none attestation to register a passkey, then log in bypassing passwords and TOTP for account takeover.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T14:54:32", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/security/advisories/GHSA-g6cq-6rqg-6c9p", "https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/security/advisories/GHSA-rg9h-f29v-xhxr", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpmyfaq-4.0.0-before-4.1.9-authentication-bypass-via-webauthn-credential-injection"], "aliases": ["GHSA-768h-xwv2-fwp3", "CVE-2026-111911"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ae7d3087-7e50-3cfd-bd1b-6f141ee35c4d", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "4.0.0 <4.1.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6284edb1-fc58-3099-b61a-d160c7f449a8", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}], "isExploited": false}